{"id":"u-4be50ee6-8588-41ed-9f13-2d45609c47bb","src":"community","title":"Optimized PHUL (Power Hypertrophy Upper Lower)","author":"Liam M.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/St7dOK-modified-phul","desc":"The goal of these revisions is to make the PHUL program more beginner-friendly by slightly altering exercise selection and rearranging the lower body days to better support recovery and sustainability. With proper attention to diet and recovery, athletes of all levels should see noticeable gains in strength and hypertrophy.\n\nDeadlifts moved to the Lower Hypertrophy Day to optimize recovery.\n\nExercise order has been adjusted to accommodate this change, and calf volume has been slightly reduced.\n\nFront squats have been replaced with Hack Squats for a better quad stimulus with less overall fatigue and a more manageable movement pattern.\n\nAb work has been added to each lower body day, which is optional but recommended for balanced core development.\n\nFor progression, aim to add either weight or reps each week. A simple method: once you hit the upper end of the rep range for a given exercise in all sets, increase the weight the next session. For Squat and Deadlift, add 10 lbs each time until you plateau, then reduce to 5 lbs increments. For Bench Press and OHP, aim to add 5 lbs each session. For accessory lifts, increase in the smallest possible increment.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":137,"rate":4,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-11-01T12:02:02.237Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper Power","Lower Power: Squat day","Upper Hypertrophy","Lower Hypertrophy: Deadlifts"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":5,"rpe":8.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"Can do incline dumbbell bench"},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":5,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"Can do regular barbe